From: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] leds: lp55xx: register LEDs with their device-tree node when a label is given

The LED class core reads per-LED properties such as "led-pattern" (pattern
trigger) from the fwnode of the LED class device, but lp55xx registers its
LEDs without one, so device-tree patterns never reach the pattern trigger.
Keep the channel node in the LED configuration and, when the node carries a
"label", register the LED with led_init_data pointing at that node. The label
becomes the LED name (unchanged for nodes whose label equals chan-name);
nodes without a label keep the old registration path.

Signed-off-by: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/platform_data/leds-lp55xx.h
+++ b/include/linux/platform_data/leds-lp55xx.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 struct lp55xx_led_config {
 	const char *name;
 	const char *default_trigger;
+	struct device_node *np;	/* DT node of the channel, if any */
 	u8 chan_nr;
 	u8 led_current; /* mA x10, 0 if led is not connected */
 	u8 max_current;
--- a/drivers/leds/leds-lp55xx-common.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-lp55xx-common.c
@@ -221,10 +221,24 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (pdata->led_config[chan].num_colors > 1)
+	if (pdata->led_config[chan].num_colors > 1) {
 		ret = devm_led_classdev_multicolor_register(dev, &led->mc_cdev);
-	else
+	} else if (pdata->led_config[chan].np &&
+		   of_find_property(pdata->led_config[chan].np, "label", NULL)) {
+		/*
+		 * Register with the channel's DT node so that the LED core can
+		 * read the node's properties, in particular "led-pattern" for
+		 * the pattern trigger. The DT "label" becomes the LED name, so
+		 * this path is only taken when a label is given.
+		 */
+		struct led_init_data init_data = {
+			.fwnode = of_fwnode_handle(pdata->led_config[chan].np),
+		};
+
+		ret = devm_led_classdev_register_ext(dev, &led->cdev, &init_data);
+	} else {
 		ret = devm_led_classdev_register(dev, &led->cdev);
+	}
 
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "led register err: %d\n", ret);
@@ -643,6 +657,7 @@
 
 	cfg[child_number].default_trigger =
 		of_get_property(np, "linux,default-trigger", NULL);
+	cfg[child_number].np = np;
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(np, "color", &led_color);
 	if (ret)
